Martin -

Thanks for your reply. Is RdbiPgSQL no longer maintained at all? I have tried RPostgreSQL, but it has an even worse problem. In that package, dbWriteTable is implemented by calling write.table on the data frame to write it to a temporary file, and then load it into the database, which means that the formatting options set in R affect the result. Specifically, write.table by default formats some numbers in scientific notation, which causes the database load to fail.

After looking into the problem with RdbiPgSQL a little more, it seems that it's caused by dbDisconnect calling the same function that is registered as the finalizer. I think it could be easily solved by using an indicator variable to keep track of whether PQfinish has been called. (I can also just call rm instead of dbDisconnect, but it's a little disconcerting that the package contains a function that causes memory errors when used as intended.)

- Elliot


