From: aryee at jhu.edu (Martin Aryee)
Date: Mon, 24 Jan 2011 12:00:37 -0500
Subject: [BioC] Application of Method of Aryee et al to Illumina methylation
	Arrays
In-Reply-To: <mailman.10.1295866804.403.bioconductor@r-project.org>
References: <mailman.10.1295866804.403.bioconductor@r-project.org>
Message-ID: <F520076E-35C5-4797-939A-01FAF219F1A4@jhu.edu>

Hi Rich,

The methods unfortunately wouldn't be suitable for Infinium arrays. The tools in this paper were developed using data from Roche (Nimblegen) microarrays and the McrBC restriction enzyme. Since the Illumina Infinium array is based on a completely different assay involving Bisulfite conversion, the methods wouldn't be applicable.

Best,
Martin.

