On 01/27/2011 04:45 PM, Ted Morrow wrote:
> Thanks for your replies Gilbert and Peter.....I forgot to say in my
> original question that I did look into using both the GeneAnswers
> package and the FunDO web-based system but the issue I have not been
> able to solve with them is that I cannot specify "my gene Universe"
> within which my selected genes are tested for enrichment. I want to see
> which diseases are enriched out of the possible diseases in "my gene
> universe" which is a subset of all possible human genes.
>
> Is that possible in GeneAnswers (or even FunDO)?
>
> Cheers
> Ted



Just as a word of caution with this analysis, I think you will get 
biased answers if you use all possible human genes as your 
universe/population. I would consider limiting the population set to all 
genes known to be associated with at least one disease (or something 
similar appropriate to your experiment). In GO analysis, if you use all 
genes as your population (rather than all genes annotated to at least 
one GO term), this tends to overestimate statistical significance.
-peter







