In-Reply-To: <loom.20110129T013615-927@post.gmane.org>
References: <loom.20110129T013615-927@post.gmane.org>
Message-ID: <4D4461AC.60909@aon.at>

Dear Addiel,

The reason is that the antigenomic.bgp file contains redundant 
information which is already present in the HuEx-1_0-st-v2.r2.pgf file.

Simply search the pgf-file for: control->bgp->antigenomic

BTW, in function rma() "antigenomic" is only a parameter which is 
internally used for the mask. Function rma() still uses the PMs only for 
background correction of exon arrays. Probably I should clarify this 
issue in the help file.

If you want to use antigenomic probes for background correction you need 
to call function bgcorrect.gc().

Best regards
Christian
